<BaseLayout title="Our Habit — Racquet Habit" description="Racquet Habit is a contemporary tennis society for people with no intention of quitting.">
  <section class="editorial-hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">Institutional record / RH-000</span>
    <h1>Entirely voluntary. <em>Mostly.</em></h1>
    <p>Racquet Habit began with a familiar lie: one more set, then we are definitely leaving.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="editorial-body">
    <aside class="editorial-aside">
      <span>Filed in Yerevan</span>
      <span>Established 2026</span>
      <span>Status: active</span>
      <span>Members: repeat players</span>
    </aside>
    <div class="editorial-copy">
      <p>We make the uniform, objects and rituals around a game that quietly reorganizes the rest of your life.</p>
      <h2>A society, not a country club.</h2>
      <p>There is no gatekeeping here, no borrowed aristocracy and no fake nostalgia. Membership begins the moment you rearrange a day for court time, inspect a weather forecast too closely or carry a racquet somewhere it has no practical reason to be.</p>
      <p>The visual language is ceremonial because the behavior already is. We string racquets with precision, repeat service motions, mark scores, book the same hour and tell ourselves there is time for another set.</p>
      <div class="principles">
        <div><h3>Ornament from the game.</h3><p>Our loops, lattices and lines come from racquet strings, ball seams and court geometry—not generic heraldry.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Humor in the small print.</h3><p>The exterior is composed. The joke arrives a moment later: no intention of quitting, recreational use became habitual.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Useful beyond court.</h3><p>Everything should earn a life outside tennis. Good fabric, precise proportion and details that do not need a racquet to make sense.</p></div>
      </div>
      <h2>The first issue.</h2>
      <p>Issue 001 establishes the working uniform: a society tee, member cap, court towel, carryall and daily vessels. Coffee and seasonal drinks will arrive through limited collaborations with makers we actually know.</p>
      <a class="button" href="/shop">Examine Issue 001 <span>↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
